(1)     2B5 :
(1)     2B5 :                    *** M and D are unsigned and read their operand through (Ri), so the
(1)     2B5 :                    *** loop works on |A| and |B| in vA and vB, keeps R2 pointing at vB
(1)     2B5 :                    *** and R3 at the constant F, and keeps the sign of A*B in R4. A and B
(1)     2B5 :                    *** stay small while a point is iterated, so every product fits in 16
(1)     2B5 :                    *** bits and M leaves R0=0, ready for D.
(1)     2B5 :
